      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the comment! But I don\u0027t think wb_ctl-\u003edone_reqs can contain elements when release_wb_ctl(wb_ctl) is called, Here is the detailed flow:\n\n1. release_wb_ctl is only called after zram_writeback_slots exits\n2. zram_writeback_slots blockingly waits for wb_ctl-\u003enum_inflight to become 0 before exiting\n3. wb_ctl-\u003enum_inflight is only decremented in zram_complete_done_reqs after a request is successfully popped from wb_ctl-\u003edone_reqs\n4. If zram_writeback_endio runs concurrently with release_wb_ctl (which can only happen when the endio thread is in the window between spin_unlock_irqrestore(\u0026wb_ctl-\u003edone_lock) and rcu_read_unlock()), the request has already been popped and processed, so done_reqs is empty and num_inflight is 0\n\nIs there anything I missed?",
